<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian T-bill rates fall.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian T-bill rates fall.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rates on 91-day Lithuanian treasury bills continued a downward trend at Tuesday's auction and the issue was oversubscribed, the country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average accepted rate was 11.08 percent, versus 12.89 percent at the last auction for 91-day paper on August 27.</p>
<p>The highest accepted rate was 12.00 percent and the lowest 9.97 percent. The 55 million litas issue was oversubscribed with bids reaching almost 67 million litas.</p>
<p>The settlement date is September 6 and the bills mature on December 6. -- Riga newsroom +3717-22 66 93</p>
</text>
